GUI modernization, Phase 5 (first slice): raw evidence disclosure on
every incident chain link - PRD U3 ("التحقق من هل كان هذا هجوماً أم
فشلاً عادياً... مع أدلة خام قابلة للفتح", verifying attack vs. ordinary
failure, with raw evidence that can be opened).

## 1. The gap

`internal/incident.Link.Evidence` (`map[string]any`, JSON `evidence,
omitempty`) has existed on the wire and on the TypeScript `IncidentLink`
type (`evidence?: Record<string, unknown>`) the whole time - confirmed
by grep before assuming it was missing entirely, not just untranslated.
`IncidentCard.tsx` never rendered it anywhere. `internal/correlate/
engine.go`'s only write site (`build()`, line ~670) always sets
`describe` (`event.Describe()`'s sentence for that specific matched
event - not the same text as the clause-level `why` already shown),
and additionally `matched_count`/`last_event_id` when a clause needed
more than one match to satisfy a `min_count`. Confirmed by grepping
`Evidence[` and `Evidence:` in `engine.go` rather than assuming the
shape from the one demo example first spotted - three keys total, not
an open-ended one.

## 2. Why this stays raw/technical rather than translated

PRD U3 calls this "أدلة خام" - *raw* evidence, not a narrative account.
`evidence.describe` is `event.Describe()`'s own English sentence for one
specific event (`internal/event/describe.go`, ~40 per-kind templates) -
a genuinely separate, much larger translation project than anything
ADR 0004 covered (which stopped at rule-level title/advice/clause-why
and the kind catalogue). Translating it here would be silent, large
scope creep disguised as one disclosure. Instead every value in this
disclosure is wrapped in `TechnicalValue` - forensic evidence shown as
what the engine actually recorded, matching how event/rule IDs and
timestamps already render, not prose meant for a general reader. This
also means the untagged-Latin-sentence scanner correctly does not flag
any of it (verified below), instead of needing a new `KNOWN_GAPS` entry.

## 3. What was built

`desktop/src/components/IncidentCard.tsx`: `EvidenceDisclosure`, a
`<details>/<summary>` per chain link, collapsed by default ("قابلة
للفتح" - can be opened, not shown unconditionally). `describe`/
`matched_count`/`last_event_id` get friendly, translated labels
(`evidence_describe_label`/`evidence_matched_count_label`/
`evidence_last_event_label`, new keys in both languages); any other key
(forward-compat for a future engine addition) falls back to showing the
raw key name in `TechnicalValue`, the same "never crash, never blank"
pattern used everywhere else in this ADR-adjacent work.

`desktop/src/components/IncidentCard.test.tsx` (new - this component
had no dedicated test file at all before this): three tests prove the
known-key labels render with their values, an unrecognised key falls
back to its raw name, and a link with no evidence renders no disclosure
at all (not an empty one).

## 4. Full regression

    $ npx tsc --noEmit                             clean
    $ npm test                                     10 files, 59 tests passed
    $ npm run build                                clean
    $ npx playwright test                          35 passed (0 failed) -
        the untagged-Latin-sentence scanner (evidence 38) found zero new
        violations, confirming the TechnicalValue-wrapping choice above
        actually avoids the scope question rather than merely intending to

## 5. Actually looked at it

Fresh browser tab against the demo recording, both languages. Every one
of the demo's 16 incidents' chain links now shows a "Raw evidence" /
"الدليل الخام" disclosure, collapsed (▶) by default. Opened one:
English shows "What happened" -> "nrlab0 lost carrier" (in monospace);
Arabic shows "ما الذي حدث" -> the same raw English value unchanged,
confirming the label translates while the forensic content deliberately
does not. Console clean in both languages.

## 6. What remains in Phase 5

This is the first slice of a large phase (execution order §9): Incidents
master/detail with search/sort/filter, Rules bilingual catalogue
improvements, Evidence's incident-scoped export with an adjustable
padding window (PRD U5), Settings regrouped into six sections with a
sticky save/discard bar, Diagnostics' secret-free support-summary copy
button. None of those are started by this slice. No new ADR needed here
- this is a pure frontend rendering addition with no contract change,
same as the earlier Button/TechnicalValue component work.
